/**
 * @defgroup MIDILAR_Workflows_PackageConsumer Installed Package Consumer Test
 * @ingroup MIDILAR_Workflows
 * @brief Validate MIDILAR exactly as an independent downstream project uses it.
 *
 * The package consumer test performs a Release export, configures the isolated
 * project in `tests/PackageConsumer`, builds it using only `MIDILAR::MIDILAR`, and runs
 * it. The consumer intentionally calls `Foundation::Math::GCD` without linking
 * `Foundation::Foundation` directly. This verifies both parts of MIDILAR's public
 * dependency contract:
 *
 * - `MIDILARConfig.cmake` locates Foundation with `find_dependency()`.
 * - `MIDILAR::MIDILAR` propagates Foundation headers and link requirements.
 *
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./scripts/test-package.sh macos_arm64 --fresh
 * @endcode
 *
 * @code{.powershell}
 * ./scripts/test-package.ps1 windows_msvc_x64 -Fresh
 * @endcode
 *
 * Use `--foundation-prefix` or `-FoundationPrefix` when Foundation is not in
 * the sibling `../Foundation/dist/<preset>` location. This workflow is for
 * runnable desktop presets; cross-compiled packages are validated separately.
 */
